{"agent":"fx-list-limit","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new `offset` parameter is inserted before the existing `all`, `mode`, and `sources` parameters in the public API function at this line. Any existing caller that passes `all` positionally, for example `ddflow.api.viewers.search_view(repo, query, kind, since, item, limit, True)`, now binds `True` to `offset` instead of `all`, so the call either skips the first row or raises an offset-past-end ViewError for small result sets. The new parameter should be added after `sources` or made keyword-only to avoid changing existing positional argument meaning.","digest":"3238b6a39d030c0f","location":"ddflow/api/viewers.py:121","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/viewers.py:121"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The reported bug is in the CLI command `ddflow list task --limit 5000 ...`, but no regression test actually runs that CLI path. This test calls `view_list()` directly and then calls the private `VL._print_rows()` on that already-rendered result, so it can pass even when the real CLI still prints the old `raise --limit` footer. Likewise, the previous CLI-level `--limit 0` test was replaced by `--limit -1`, while the new positive zero-limit test only calls the API, not `run_cli(... \"task\", \"list\", \"--limit\", \"0\")`. The exact command from the bug report is never exercised.","digest":"b076d59bee09f87c","location":"tests/test_list_limit.py:37 `test_text_footer_names_the_cap_and_the_next_offset`","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_list_limit.py:37 `test_text_footer_names_the_cap_and_the_next_offset`"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":12791,"diff_sha":"601f8ef9d6b04b75727465fa4097a6d0fe6e3393960959aa307830004e81b7e2","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":885.4,"excluded_bytes":1