{"agent":"fx-list-limit","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new `offset` parameter is accepted by `read`, whose doc says it is the one read over every viewer including `search`, but the diff only forwards `offset` to the `list_view` call at line 173. For `mode=\"search\"`, `offset` is silently ignored: `read(repo, mode=\"search\", limit=100, offset=500)` on a repo with >500 matches returns the first 100 rows rather than rows 500–599 and raises no error, so the advertised parameter does not work for one of the viewers it claims to cover.","digest":"7f4a6daaf3f0f0e1","location":"ddflow/api/viewers.py:122 read","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/viewers.py:122 read"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"When a list is truncated, the new hint `next page: --offset {d['next']}` omits the current `--limit`. Since `--limit` defaults to `R.LIST_DEFAULT_LIMIT` (25), a user who runs the displayed hint after a non-default limit gets a different page size. Example: `ddflow list task --limit 50` with 2720 rows prints `next page: --offset 50`; running `ddflow list task --offset 50` shows only 25 rows, not the next 50. The clamped case from the bug is equally misleading: after `--limit 5000` the hint says `next page: --offset 1000`, but running that without the clamped limit gives the default 25-row page. The hint should include `--limit {d['limit']}`.","digest":"fb57c01265ead93c","location":"ddflow/surfaces/commands/viewers_lists.py:_print_rows","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/surfaces/commands/viewers_lists.py:_print_rows"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":14143,"diff_sha":"e4f3a1e04af98a90d24c09371ad0047b85206204126d243cde72dd74d6b61295","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":691.0,"excluded_bytes":16486,"excluded_files":4,"excluded_paths":["README.m